---
config:
  flowchart:
    nodeSpacing: 24
---
flowchart TB
    accTitle: What the contract tests check against a real Paperless
    accDescr: run-contract.sh starts a real Paperless-ngx, the last release of 2.x or the current release of 3.x, next to Nextcloud. contract.py seeds Paperless through its REST API and checks every answer that the app reads, then the app runs its export, a move, the trash and the inbox against it. The answers of Paperless become the fixtures of the unit tests in tests/fixtures/, which PaperlessApiServiceTest reads; a later run compares their shapes with the fixtures and fails when a field that the tests read is gone. Every Monday a failure opens an issue.

    run["run-contract.sh 2 or 3"]
    subgraph compose ["Docker Compose project"]
        contract["contract.py<br>seeds Paperless and<br>checks each answer"]
        nextcloud["Nextcloud<br>this checkout<br>as a custom app"]
        paperless["Paperless-ngx<br>2.20 or 3.x,<br>with Redis"]
    end
    fixtures[("tests/fixtures/<br>paperless-ngx-2,<br>paperless-ngx-3")]
    unit["PaperlessApiServiceTest<br>reads the answers<br>of Paperless"]
    issue["Every Monday:<br>an issue when<br>Paperless answers<br>differently"]

    run --> contract
    run -- "export, move,<br>trash, inbox" --> nextcloud
    contract -- "REST API" --> paperless
    nextcloud -- "REST API,<br>version 9" --> paperless
    contract -- "answers,<br>CONTRACT_RECORD=1" --> fixtures
    fixtures -- "shapes compared<br>in every run" --> contract
    fixtures --> unit
    run -. "failure" .-> issue

    classDef nextcloud fill:#0082c92e,stroke:#0082c9,stroke-width:2px
    classDef paperless fill:#17803d2e,stroke:#17803d,stroke-width:2px
    classDef data fill:#f59e0b2e,stroke:#f59e0b,stroke-width:2px
    class nextcloud nextcloud
    class paperless,contract paperless
    class fixtures,unit data
